  "body": "## Summary\n\n```text\nrequest \u2192 project-local router \u2192 frozen embedded guide \u2192 fixture conversation\n  \u2192 actual CLI verification \u2192 Recap\n  \u2192 complete-batch validity \u2192 blind/scripted grades \u2192 skill-creator viewer\n```\n\nHarness-only split from #257. No guide/router changes or new dependencies. Material AI assistance was used. Concurrent audit work is preserved through `16571438`; follow-up fixes are pushed in `2a2a83f6`.\n\n- Fail-closed macOS shell boundary; no bypassPermissions, live Project or real Docker execution. Synthetic media metadata, no pretend movie payloads; unmodeled machine probes are refused.\n- Owned model process-group cleanup on failure, timeout and signals. Retained frozen inputs/raw diagnostics; failed, malformed, unfinished and quota-limited attempts never become scores.\n- Stale grades/verdicts are invalidated; blind judgments are fingerprinted. Runtime identifiers don't reveal configuration labels.\n- Production-shaped credential/Debug/publication fixtures retain selected Apps, Recipe attribution, current Addresses and fallback Access.\n- Installation ends after successful CLI verification and Recap; optional browser/library follow-ups are declined. Verification must follow the latest mutation attempt, including host/Docker stop/disable. Separate blind Recap assessment leaves original assertion totals unchanged.\n- Guarded fixture Python resolves directly through already-required Command Line Tools, without broadening metadata permissions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** seven actual shell regressions failed because macOS's Python launcher required a forbidden developer-selection metadata read. Six runner subcases falsely accepted earlier Status after service stop/disable attempts.\n  **After:** direct CLT Python PATH and shared host-change classification pass all **60 existing offline tests**, Ruff lint/format and Pyright, including extensionless stubs. Both independent review axes rechecked and cleared their findings. No new testcases/files, dependencies or production contracts.\n- Concurrent audit commits also passed the documented Go formatting/build/vet/tests/race and installer-syntax gate; no Docker runtime, installer execution or live Project.\n- Historical iterations 9/11 scored **11/12 revised vs 10/12 original** for their frozen smoke inputs. They do not establish acceptance of the current harness; grades and caveats remain unchanged.\n- Iterations 10/12 are retained, invalid and ungraded. Iteration 12 completed only 6/42 and exposed simulation drift; no partial benchmark was accepted.\n- User approved the Recap boundary and continuing the comparison. Authentication status confirmed existing first-party Claude Pro login without API-key/custom-endpoint use. Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5 preflights passed. Fresh iteration 13 smoke is running with unchanged snapshots and equal 16-turn budgets; at most one 42-run batch follows if execution/judgments are valid. No paid fallback, model switch or billing change.\n\nFull ledger and limitations: `evals/self-host/PROGRESS.md`. Raw attempts remain outside Git and require redaction before sharing.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** development\n\nKeep draft until complete current-input execution, complete blind judgments, supplied aggregation/viewer and human feedback pass. Debian/Mint/WSL remain platform simulations, not native proofs. Refusing probes is not full machine virtualization; Claude transport is outside OS containment. Writable fixture state/logs and deliberately detached hostile code are not tamper-proof. Approval labels establish timing, not complete authorization scope. Fixture outcomes do not prove real App installation or browser acceptance.\n",
